WEBVTT

00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:20,000
I will be away from home July 19 to August 72, just I take my wife with me, I will be in hotels,

00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
I'll be flying from Turkey to Switzerland. What do you tell the agents? Yeah, we've had this

00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,160
question lots of times in the past, it really depends on a couple of things. If you're doing really

00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:38,640
well and you're going to go on a two week vacation, you're doing fantastic. You could certainly do without

00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:46,240
your right for two weeks. If you're really struggling and your health is kind of on the precipice and

00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:51,280
your had this family vacation plan for a long time, then I would take my right with me.

00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:59,520
But it can be a hassle to travel with, especially if you're overseas in other countries.

00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:04,880
For the person, I know the person who asked this question, I'd say just leave your right at home.

00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:09,920
That's my suggestion. But if someone else asks this question pretend that they were traveling to

00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:14,000
other countries like this, I'd still say it's probably better to leave your right at home if you're

00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,440
going to bring it through customs each time when you go through to another country.

00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:25,440
If you're traveling in the United States and your, you know, your health isn't like perfect,

00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:30,400
you're not in full remission, I would say bring your right with. You don't have any issues

00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:36,400
traveling with it on the airplane domestically and all, you don't have to tell them anything,

00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:44,480
domestic travel. But if you're in remission and you're going on a trip for a week, then by all means

00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:52,080
you can leave your right at home for a week.

